b.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730#issuecomment-1363172008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730","id":1363172008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85RQFqo","user":{"login":"chenrui333","id":1580956,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODA5NTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1580956?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333","html_url":"https://github.com/chenrui333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chenrui333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-22T17:42:08Z","updated_at":"2022-12-22T17:42:08Z","body":"This is the only one that I found under amzn org, https://github.com/amzn/sample-fire-tv-app-video-skill/blob/master/LICENSE.md\r\n\r\nThere are many others in this code search, https://github.com/search?q=This+Amazon+Software+License+%28%22License%22%29+governs+your+use%2C+reproduction&ref=opensearch&type=code","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1363172008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366021158","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730#issuecomment-1366021158","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730","id":1366021158,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Ra9Qm","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-27T16:18:22Z","updated_at":"2022-12-27T16:18:22Z","body":"Here's my take on how I think this one fares under the [license inclusion principles](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md). Other participants in the SPDX legal team, please weigh in as well.\r\n\r\n# New submission review\r\n\r\n* **Has the license been approved by the OSI?** _All OSI-approved license will be included on the SPDX License List, regardless of other factors_\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [X] No\r\n\r\n## Definitive Factors\r\n\r\n_These must all be satisfied to allow inclusion in the license list_\r\n\r\n1. **Is the submitted license unique, that is, it does not match another license already on the License List as per the [matching guidelines](https://spdx.org/spdx-license-list/matching-guidelines)?**\r\n    - [X] Yes\r\n    - [ ] No\r\n1. **If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?**\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [ ] No\r\n    - [X] => Unclear. By its terms, I don't see anything in here that would prevent the license from being used with executables. But the comments in this thread appear to indicate that it has only been used with executables so far.\r\n1. **Does the license have identifiable and stable text, and is not in the midst of drafting?**\r\n    - [X] Yes => See https://aws.amazon.com/asl/ which states that this is the version since 2008. Note that the version on that page does not include the preamble from the submitted version: \"This Amazon Software License (“License”) governs your use, reproduction, and distribution of the accompanying software as specified below.\"\r\n    - [ ] No\r\n1. **Has the license steward, if any, committed to versioning new versions and to not modify it after addition to the list?**\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [X] No => @MarkAtwood might weigh in here\r\n\r\n## Other factors for inclusion\r\n\r\n*Roughly in order of descending importance*\r\n\r\n1. **Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions? (examples include the [Open Source Definition](https://opensource.org/osd) and the [Debian Free Software Guidelines](https://www.debian.org/social_contract#guidelines))** (_Approval by the organisation that publishes the definition is not required_)\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [X] No => Section 3.3 prohibits use of the code other than to interact with Amazon / AWS services.\r\n1. **Is the license structured to be generally usable by anyone, and not specific to one organisation or project?**\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [X] No => Same comment as above re: Section 3.3\r\n1. **Does the license have substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (ie. use in many projects, or in one significant project)?** (_For recently written licenses, definitive plans for it to be used in at least one or a few significant projects may satisfy this_)\r\n    - [X] Yes => The AWS tools listed here are probably widely enough used to count as substantial use\r\n    - [ ] No\r\n1. **Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?**\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [X] No => Same comment as above re: Section 3.3. Even though the content itself (the \"Work\") can be freely redistributed, I don't see how \"may only use with Amazon / AWS\" can be seen as \"limited restrictions\".\r\n1. **Does the license steward support this submission, or is at least aware of and not in opposition of it?**\r\n    - [ ] Yes\r\n    - [ ] No\r\n    - [X] Unclear => @MarkAtwood might weigh in, or might not feel the need to, given the comments above.\r\n\r\n## Summary of factors, outcome, comments\r\n\r\nI'm opposed to adding this one. Given the use restriction in 3.3 limiting this to use solely with Amazon / AWS, this isn't appropriate to add to the license list. \r\n\r\nAmazon might choose to institute a standard LicenseRef for use with this license (in fact, I think that might have been one of the original use cases for the license namespace idea that @MarkAtwood had suggested) but that would not involve adding this to the SPDX License List.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366021158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366022305","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730#issuecomment-1366022305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1730","id":1366022305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Ra9ih","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id